=== p2-windows · W7 · page:admin/ApiPlayground (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:admin/ApiPlayground   kind=page   web route=/api-playground
Web source  : web/src/features/admin/pages/ApiPlaygroundPage.tsx
Output      : apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/ApiPlaygroundPage/ (+ NavigationView registration, test, ledger)
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- Layout mapping: the repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files). Every feature surface lives
  under apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.ViewModel.cs (INotifyPropertyChanged state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent
  view), exactly as the sibling W7 ApiLogsPage / StatusApiDocsPage do. The generated prompt's idealized
  "TeslaSync/Features/Admin/ApiPlaygroundPage.xaml + ApiPlaygroundPageViewModel.cs" is mapped onto these real
  conventions. Namespace = TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews.Admin (aligns with RouteGroup.AdminDevTools).
- Data binding (ADR-004): the manifest declares NO API data sources ("renders from navigation params / local
  state"). The web page actually fetches /system/openapi via useQuery, but the generated C# client exposes no
  parsed-OpenAPI-catalog endpoint — so, following the established ApiLogsPage precedent, the page is driven by an
  injected IApiPlaygroundFeed. The default CatalogApiPlaygroundFeed resolves a static catalog of the documented
  TeslaSync API endpoints (the native source-of-truth mirror of internal/api/router.go, exactly as
  StatusApiDocsPage ships its 6 status endpoints), so the populated success state renders without a network
  round-trip; EmptyApiPlaygroundFeed (and a host-supplied live-spec feed) keep the loading/empty/error states
  genuinely reachable and unit-tested. ApiPlaygroundPageViewModel.LoadAsync/RefreshAsync honour the page
  lifecycle (OnLoaded → LoadAsync); SetQuery/SelectEndpoint/ClearSelection re-project without a reload.
- Four data states (manifest: loading/empty/error/success), ApiPlaygroundProjection.ResolveState:
  · loading — catalog feed in flight with nothing loaded yet → the sidebar renders a Fluent skeleton (web the
    EndpointSidebar Skeleton rows). ApiPlaygroundState.Loading.
  · empty  — the catalog (or the active search) yielded no rows → a friendly TsEmptyState (web
    playground.noResults "No matching endpoints"), never a blank region (ADR-011). ApiPlaygroundState.Empty.
  · error  — the feed threw → an inline TsErrorDisplay with a Retry affordance wired to RefreshAsync (web the
    PageContainer error branch; ADR-013 surfacing). ApiPlaygroundState.Error.
  · success— ≥1 row → the tag-grouped, selectable endpoint list. ApiPlaygroundState.Success.
- Panels (ADR-005), the manifest's two GlassPanel slots (web ApiPlaygroundPage.tsx, the two <GlassPanel>s):
  · GlassPanel1 = the w-72 sidebar. A TsGlassPanel hosting a TsInput search box (web the EndpointSidebar search;
    playground.search) over a scrollable list rendered by state (skeleton | error+retry | empty | grouped rows).
    Each row is a TsButton (Subtle; Secondary when selected) carrying a method TsBadge (StatusKind: GET=Info,
    POST=Success, mutate=Warning, DELETE=Danger) + the mono path, grouped under tag headers (web the
    EndpointSidebar tag sections, sorted by tag → method weight → path).
  · GlassPanel2 = the main panel. With no selection it shows the BookOpen TsEmptyState prompt
    (playground.selectEndpoint) and, when the catalog is non-empty, the "{n} endpoints available" caption
    (playground.endpointCount, formatted via string.Format). With a selection it shows the endpoint detail
    (method badge + mono path + tag + summary + description + grouped Path/Query parameters) — the native
    analogue of the web RequestBuilder header (never a blank box, ADR-011).
  No hardcoded colours/typography — DisplayTokens (TsColorText*/Border/TsTypeFontFamilyMono) drive
  light/dark/high-contrast from W1.
- Header (web PageContainer title/subtitle): the shared native PageContainer surface carries the
  heading-level-1 title (playground.title) + muted subtitle (playground.subtitle).
- Navigation entry: RouteTable.cs already maps Page("ApiPlayground","api-playground",RouteGroup.AdminDevTools)
  — unchanged. ShellWindow.xaml.cs registers the page factory next to ApiLogs
  (new FeatureViews.Admin.ApiPlaygroundPage()). This page introduces NO new route.
- i18n (ADR-014): the four manifest keys (playground.title/subtitle/selectEndpoint/endpointCount) plus the
  feature's sibling keys (playground.search/noResults/pathParams/queryParams) ALREADY EXIST in the
  AUTO-GENERATED catalog Strings/en|ar|he/Resources.resw ("do not edit by hand") as translation.playground.*.
  Per the established ApiLogsPage/StatusApiDocsPage precedent every literal is resolved through
  ILocalizer.GetString("playground.<key>", englishFallback) using the bare web key names; absent/locale keys
  resolve to the verbatim web English copy via the ShellLocalizer → ResourceLoader bridge. Zero hardcoded UI
  text; zero hand-edit of the generated catalog. The few introduced labels (loadError/retry/required/optional)
  carry English fallbacks, mirroring how StatusApiDocs introduced statusApiDocs.empty/back.
- a11y (ADR-015): AutomationProperties names on the page (title), the sidebar (Navigation landmark) and the main
  panel (Main landmark + the selected endpoint's method+path+summary); each endpoint row carries a method+path
  Narrator name + summary tooltip; decorative glyphs set AccessibilityView=Raw; a Group automation peer;
  light/dark/high-contrast via the W1 tokens; TsButton/TsInput keyboard + pointer for free.
- Units (ADR-005/P1-S5): the page documents an API contract and renders no measured quantities, so no unit
  conversion is involved.

PRE-EXECUTION FINDING (environment setup — build-blocking at baseline, NOT caused by this change):
- TeslaSync.App.Core and TeslaSync.App.Tests ProjectReference ..\Generated\Generated.csproj — the W1/ADR-004
  generated OpenAPI C# client. apps/windows/Generated/ is GITIGNORED (.gitignore `apps/**/generated/`) — a
  regenerated, not-committed artifact — and was ABSENT in this fresh worktree, so the solution did not build
  (CS0234 "TeslaSync.Windows does not exist"). It is produced by apps/tools/codegen/gen-clients.ts. Ran
  `pwsh apps/tools/codegen/gen-clients.ps1` → emitted 10 C# records to apps/windows/Generated/Api/. The emitter
  writes only the Api/*.cs records (no project file), so a thin local Generated/Generated.csproj shim (net10,
  compiles Api/*.cs into TeslaSync.Windows.Generated.Api, mirroring apps/tools/codegen/verify/csharp/Verify.csproj)
  was created so Core/Tests resolve the client. Both apps/windows/Generated/Api/*.cs AND that csproj are gitignored
  and are therefore NOT part of this commit — pure local build setup of the W1 predecessor.

